  "details": "Witmotion trackers are budget friendly, but I don't know how to program for tracker software, otherwise, I would have done it and published it. I'll personally be happy to be test subject to make it work, I even have two sensors, and plenty of time for you to specifically throw experimental updates at me.\n\nWitmotion trackers provide an amazing way to seriously enhance gameplay for users who are only able to use camera expressions, as we all know the tracker will fail if hands are not visible. I mean, the trackers are sensitive enough to detect my heartbeat, they cost like $60 each\n\nI'd heavily recommend taking advantage of the dongle mode in full, and allow users to program in multiple sensors(the dongle adapter does not appear to support more than one sensor connection at a time, each sensor will take a physical slot)....if they have the plugs for it, why not.\n\nPlease add witmotion as a sensor option, they provide developer documentation so they can be customized.",
